module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ChartImmersionFinish.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Conormal.ConormalSequenceMiddle
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjShared.RelevantCover

/-!
# The affine charts and the degree-one coordinates of Stacks Tag 02NP

The proof of [Stacks, Tag 02NP] opens by reading the very ampleness hypothesis as an immersion
`α : X ⟶ Proj A` over an affine base; its remaining argument is a *choice*, in two steps:

1. cover `X` by the finitely many affine opens `α⁻¹(D₊(f_j))` on which `α` is a closed immersion,
   and write the algebra generators of each `Γ(X, α⁻¹(D₊(f_j)))` over the base as fractions
   `f_{j,k} / f_j^{e}`;
2. choose finitely many degree-one elements `y_0, …, y_n` of `A` in which every `f_j` and every
   `f_{j,k}` is a polynomial over the base.

This file performs both choices. Neither is specific to `A = Γ(S, Sym(E))`: the first holds for an
immersion into the homogeneous spectrum of any graded ring, and the second is pure algebra.

## Main results

* `Stacks.CoordinateChoice.exists_finset_subset_adjoin`: **an element of a subalgebra generated by
  a set already lies in the subalgebra generated by a finite subset of it.**
* `Stacks.CoordinateChoice.exists_fin_mem_adjoin_range`: **step 2.** If `A` is generated over `R`
  by its degree-one part then any finite set of elements of `A` lies in the subalgebra generated
  by finitely many degree-one elements, indexed by a `Fin (n + 1)`.
* `Stacks.CoordinateChoice.exists_basicOpen_le_coborderRange`: a point of the source of an
  immersion into `Proj A` has a relevant standard open `D₊(g)` around its image inside the
  coborder of the range, so that `α` restricts to a **closed** immersion over it
  (`Stacks.CoordinateChoice.isClosedImmersion_restrict_basicOpen`).
* `Stacks.CoordinateChoice.exists_fin_basicOpen_cover_le_coborderRange`: **step 1's cover.** For
  a quasi-compact source, finitely many such standard opens already cover.
* `Stacks.CoordinateChoice.isAffineOpen_preimage_basicOpen` and
  `Stacks.CoordinateChoice.surjective_app_basicOpen`: the chart `α⁻¹(D₊(g))` of such a standard
  open is **affine**, and every one of its sections is the image of a section of `D₊(g)` — by
  `Stacks.CoordinateChoice.surjective_awayToChart`, of a fraction `b / g^k`.
* `Stacks.CoordinateChoice.exists_finset_away_forall_mem_closure`: **the rest of step 1.** Over an
  affine open of the base the sections of the chart are generated, as a ring, by the sections
  coming from the base together with finitely many fractions `b / g^k`. This is [Stacks, Tag 01T2]
  at the chart.
* `Stacks.CoordinateChoice.mem_span_of_mem_adjoin`,
  `Stacks.CoordinateChoice.basicOpen_le_iSup_basicOpen_of_mem_adjoin` and
  `Stacks.CoordinateChoice.exists_mem_preimage_basicOpen_of_mem_adjoin`: **the chosen coordinates
  cover the charts they were chosen for.** A homogeneous element of positive degree in the
  subalgebra generated over `A₀` by the `y_i` lies in the ideal they span, so its standard open is
  covered by theirs — hence the charts `α⁻¹(D₊(y_i))` cover `X` as soon as the charts
  `α⁻¹(D₊(g_j))` do. This is the generation clause of
  `Stacks.VeryAmpleAffineBase.ProjCoordinateImmersion` at the source's coordinates.

## Implementation notes

The cover is cut out of `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.coborderRange`, the largest open in which
the range of an immersion is closed: a standard open inside it restricts the immersion to a closed
immersion (`AlgebraicGeometry.isClosedImmersion_resLE_of_le_coborderRange`), and the relevant
standard opens — those of a homogeneous element of *positive* degree, the only ones that are
affine — form a basis of `Proj A` by
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjShared.isBasis_basicOpen_homogeneous`. So the two facts meet
with nothing in between, and the degrees of the `f_j` are whatever the basis hands back — which is
exactly why the source's second step, the passage to degree one, is needed at all.

`Stacks.CoordinateChoice.exists_fin_mem_adjoin_range` pads the chosen degree-one elements with
`0` to be indexed by a `Fin (n + 1)`, as the morphism to `ℙⁿ_S` that consumes them is pinned by a
family of that shape; `0` is in every graded piece, so the padding is harmless.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 02NP](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02NP)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01M5](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01M5)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01T2](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01T2)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory TopologicalSpace

universe u w

namespace Stacks.CoordinateChoice

/-! ### Finitely many generators suffice for finitely many elements -/

/-- **An element of the subalgebra generated by a set lies in the subalgebra generated by a finite
subset of it.** -/
theorem exists_finset_subset_adjoin {R A : Type*} [CommSemiring R] [CommSemiring A] [Algebra R A]
    {s : Set A} {x : A} (hx : x ∈ Algebra.adjoin R s) :
    ∃ u : Finset A, ↑u ⊆ s ∧ x ∈ Algebra.adjoin R (u : Set A) := by
  classical
  induction hx using Algebra.adjoin_induction with
  | mem a ha => exact ⟨{a}, by simpa using ha, Algebra.subset_adjoin (by simp)⟩
  | algebraMap r => exact ⟨∅, by simp, Subalgebra.algebraMap_mem _ r⟩
  | add x y _ _ ihx ihy =>
    obtain ⟨u, hu, hxu⟩ := ihx
    obtain ⟨v, hv, hyv⟩ := ihy
    exact ⟨u ∪ v, by simp [hu, hv],
      add_mem (Algebra.adjoin_mono (by simp) hxu) (Algebra.adjoin_mono (by simp) hyv)⟩
  | mul x y _ _ ihx ihy =>
    obtain ⟨u, hu, hxu⟩ := ihx
    obtain ⟨v, hv, hyv⟩ := ihy
    exact ⟨u ∪ v, by simp [hu, hv],
      mul_mem (Algebra.adjoin_mono (by simp) hxu) (Algebra.adjoin_mono (by simp) hyv)⟩

/-- **The degree-one coordinates of [Stacks, Tag 02NP].** If the graded ring `A` is generated over
`R` by its degree-one part, then every finite set of elements of `A` consists of polynomials over
`R` in finitely many degree-one elements.

The family is indexed by a `Fin (n + 1)` because that is the shape of a family of sections pinning
a morphism to `ℙⁿ`; the padding element is `0`, which lies in every graded piece. -/
theorem exists_fin_mem_adjoin_range {R : Type*} {A : Type u} {σ : Type w} [CommRing R]
    [CommRing A] [Algebra R A] [SetLike σ A] [AddSubgroupClass σ A] (𝒜 : ℕ → σ)
    (hgen : Algebra.adjoin R ((𝒜 1 : σ) : Set A) = ⊤) (T : Finset A) :
    ∃ (n : ℕ) (y : Fin (n + 1) → A), (∀ i, y i ∈ 𝒜 1) ∧
      ∀ t ∈ T, t ∈ Algebra.adjoin R (Set.range y) := by
  classical
  have hsub : ∀ t : A, ∃ u : Finset A, ↑u ⊆ ((𝒜 1 : σ) : Set A) ∧
      t ∈ Algebra.adjoin R (u : Set A) :=
    fun t => exists_finset_subset_adjoin (by rw [hgen]; exact Algebra.mem_top)
  choose u hu hmem using hsub
  set U : Finset A := T.biUnion u with hU
  obtain ⟨m, ⟨eqv⟩⟩ := Finite.exists_equiv_fin ↥U
  set y : Fin (m + 1) → A := Fin.lastCases 0 fun k => (eqv.symm k : A) with hy
  have hyval : ∀ (a : A) (ha : a ∈ U), y (eqv ⟨a, ha⟩).castSucc = a := by
    intro a ha
    simp only [hy, Fin.lastCases_castSucc, Equiv.symm_apply_apply]
  refine ⟨m, y, fun i => ?_, fun t ht => ?_⟩
  · refine Fin.lastCases ?_ (fun k => ?_) i
    · simpa only [hy, Fin.lastCases_last] using zero_mem (𝒜 1)
    · obtain ⟨t, _, hau⟩ := Finset.mem_biUnion.mp (eqv.symm k).2
      simpa only [hy, Fin.lastCases_castSucc, SetLike.mem_coe] using hu t hau
  · refine Algebra.adjoin_mono (fun a ha => ?_) (hmem t)
    have haU : a ∈ U := Finset.mem_biUnion.mpr ⟨t, ht, ha⟩
    exact ⟨(eqv ⟨a, haU⟩).castSucc, hyval a haU⟩

/-! ### The chosen coordinates cover what they generate -/

section Span

variable {A : Type u} {σ : Type w} [CommRing A] [SetLike σ A] [AddSubgroupClass σ A]
  (𝒜 : ℕ → σ) [GradedRing 𝒜]

/-- **An element of the subalgebra generated over `A₀` by homogeneous elements differs from its
degree-zero part by an element of the ideal they span.**

This is the induction inside Mathlib's `AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.iSup_basicOpen_eq_top'`, which that
proof does not expose: there the family generates all of `A`, here it generates only a
subalgebra. The multiplicative step works because `GradedRing.projZeroRingHom` is a ring
homomorphism: `ab - (ab)₀ = a(b - b₀) + (a - a₀)b₀`. -/
theorem sub_projZero_mem_span_of_mem_adjoin {ι : Type*} (y : ι → A) (hy : ∀ i, ∃ n, y i ∈ 𝒜 n)
    {a : A} (ha : a ∈ Algebra.adjoin (𝒜 0) (Set.range y)) :
    a - GradedRing.projZeroRingHom 𝒜 a ∈ Ideal.span (Set.range y) := by
  induction ha using Algebra.adjoin_induction with
  | mem x hx =>
    obtain ⟨i, rfl⟩ := hx
    obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := hy i
    rw [GradedRing.projZeroRingHom_apply]
    by_cases hn' : n = 0
    · rw [DirectSum.decompose_of_mem_same 𝒜 (hn' ▸ hn), sub_self]
      exact zero_mem _
    · rw [DirectSum.decompose_of_mem_ne 𝒜 hn hn', sub_zero]
      exact Ideal.subset_span ⟨_, rfl⟩
  | algebraMap r =>
    convert! zero_mem (Ideal.span _)
    rw [sub_eq_zero]
    exact (DirectSum.decompose_of_mem_same 𝒜 r.2).symm
  | add x y hx hy _ _ =>
    rw [map_add, add_sub_add_comm]
    exact add_mem ‹_› ‹_›
  | mul x y hx hy hx' hy' =>
    convert!
      add_mem (Ideal.mul_mem_left _ x hy')
        (Ideal.mul_mem_right (GradedRing.projZeroRingHom 𝒜 y) _ hx') using 1
    rw [map_mul]
    ring

/-- **A homogeneous element of positive degree in the subalgebra generated over `A₀` by
homogeneous elements lies in the ideal they span.** Its degree-zero part is zero, so
`Stacks.CoordinateChoice.sub_projZero_mem_span_of_mem_adjoin` is the statement itself. -/
theorem mem_span_of_mem_adjoin {ι : Type*} (y : ι → A) (hy : ∀ i, ∃ n, y i ∈ 𝒜 n) {d : ℕ}
    (hd : 0 < d) {g : A} (hg : g ∈ 𝒜 d)
    (hmem : g ∈ Algebra.adjoin (𝒜 0) (Set.range y)) :
    g ∈ Ideal.span (Set.range y) := by
  have h := sub_projZero_mem_span_of_mem_adjoin 𝒜 y hy hmem
  rwa [GradedRing.projZeroRingHom_apply, DirectSum.decompose_of_mem_ne 𝒜 hg hd.ne',
    sub_zero] at h

/-- **The standard opens of a family cover the standard open of anything in the ideal it spans.**
-/
theorem basicOpen_le_iSup_basicOpen_of_mem_span {ι : Type*} (y : ι → A) {g : A}
    (hg : g ∈ Ideal.span (Set.range y)) :
    AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 g ≤ ⨆ i, AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (y i) := by
  intro p hp
  rw [AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.mem_basicOpen] at hp
  rw [TopologicalSpace.Opens.mem_iSup]
  by_contra hcon
  simp only [not_exists, AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.mem_basicOpen, not_not] at hcon
  exact hp (Ideal.span_le.mpr (Set.range_subset_iff.mpr hcon) hg)

/-- **The degree-one coordinates of [Stacks, Tag 02NP] cover the charts they were chosen for.**
The standard open of a homogeneous element `g` of positive degree lying in the subalgebra
generated over `A₀` by a family of homogeneous elements covers nothing new: it is contained in the
union of their standard opens. -/
theorem basicOpen_le_iSup_basicOpen_of_mem_adjoin {ι : Type*} (y : ι → A)
    (hy : ∀ i, ∃ n, y i ∈ 𝒜 n) {d : ℕ} (hd : 0 < d) {g : A} (hg : g ∈ 𝒜 d)
    (hmem : g ∈ Algebra.adjoin (𝒜 0) (Set.range y)) :
    AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 g ≤ ⨆ i, AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (y i) :=
  basicOpen_le_iSup_basicOpen_of_mem_span 𝒜 y (mem_span_of_mem_adjoin 𝒜 y hy hd hg hmem)

end Span

/-! ### The affine charts on which the immersion is closed -/

section Cover

variable {A : Type u} {σ : Type w} [CommRing A] [SetLike σ A] [AddSubgroupClass σ A]
  (𝒜 : ℕ → σ) [GradedRing 𝒜] {X : Scheme.{u}} (α : X ⟶ AlgebraicGeometry.Proj 𝒜) [IsImmersion α]

/-- **Around the image of any point of `X` there is a relevant standard open of `Proj A` inside
the coborder of the range of `α`.** On such an open `α` restricts to a closed immersion
(`Stacks.CoordinateChoice.isClosedImmersion_restrict_basicOpen`), and the open is affine because
its element is homogeneous of positive degree. -/
theorem exists_basicOpen_le_coborderRange (x : X) :
    ∃ (d : ℕ) (g : A), 0 < d ∧ g ∈ 𝒜 d ∧ x ∈ α ⁻¹ᵁ AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 g ∧
      AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 g ≤ α.coborderRange := by
  have hx : α.base x ∈ α.coborderRange := subset_coborder (Set.mem_range_self x)
  obtain ⟨d, g, hd, hg, hxg, hle⟩ :=
    Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjShared.exists_basicOpen_homogeneous_le 𝒜 hx
  exact ⟨d, g, hd, hg, hxg, hle⟩

/-- **Step 1 of what [Stacks, Tag 02NP] still owes: the finite affine cover.** For `X`
quasi-compact, finitely many relevant standard opens `D₊(g_j)` of `Proj A` lie inside the coborder
of the range of `α` and have preimages covering `X`.

This is the source's "choose a finite affine open cover `X = ⋃ U_j` with `U_j = α⁻¹(D₊(f_j))` and
`α|U_j` a closed immersion": the closed immersion is
`Stacks.CoordinateChoice.isClosedImmersion_restrict_basicOpen` and the affineness of each `U_j` is
`Stacks.CoordinateChoice.isAffineOpen_preimage_basicOpen`. -/
theorem exists_fin_basicOpen_cover_le_coborderRange [CompactSpace X] :
    ∃ (m : ℕ) (d : Fin m → ℕ) (g : Fin m → A), (∀ j, 0 < d j) ∧ (∀ j, g j ∈ 𝒜 (d j)) ∧
      (∀ x : X, ∃ j, x ∈ α ⁻¹ᵁ AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (g j)) ∧
      ∀ j, AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (g j) ≤ α.coborderRange := by
  classical
  choose d g hd hg hx hcob using exists_basicOpen_le_coborderRange 𝒜 α
  obtain ⟨T, hT⟩ : ∃ T : Finset X, (Set.univ : Set X) ⊆
      ⋃ z ∈ T, ((α ⁻¹ᵁ AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (g z) : X.Opens) : Set X) :=
    isCompact_univ.elim_finite_subcover
      (fun z : X => ((α ⁻¹ᵁ AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (g z) : X.Opens) : Set X))
      (fun z => (α ⁻¹ᵁ AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (g z)).isOpen)
      (fun z _ => Set.mem_iUnion.mpr ⟨z, hx z⟩)
  obtain ⟨m, ⟨eqv⟩⟩ := Finite.exists_equiv_fin ↥T
  refine ⟨m, fun j => d (eqv.symm j), fun j => g (eqv.symm j), fun j => hd _, fun j => hg _,
    fun z => ?_, fun j => hcob _⟩
  obtain ⟨w, hwT, hw⟩ := Set.mem_iUnion₂.mp (hT (Set.mem_univ z))
  refine ⟨eqv ⟨w, hwT⟩, ?_⟩
  simp only [Equiv.symm_apply_apply]
  exact hw

/-- **Over a standard open inside the coborder of its range the immersion is a closed
immersion.** -/
theorem isClosedImmersion_restrict_basicOpen {g : A}
    (hcob : AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 g ≤ α.coborderRange) :
    IsClosedImmersion (α ∣_ AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 g) := by
  have h := AlgebraicGeometry.isClosedImmersion_resLE_of_le_coborderRange α _ hcob
  rwa [Scheme.Hom.resLE_eq_morphismRestrict] at h

/-- **The chart of a relevant standard open inside the coborder is affine.** A closed immersion
into an affine scheme has affine source, and `D₊(g)` is affine for `g` homogeneous of positive
degree. -/
theorem isAffineOpen_preimage_basicOpen {d : ℕ} {g : A} (hg : g ∈ 𝒜 d) (hd : 0 < d)
    (hcob : AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 g ≤ α.coborderRange) :
    IsAffineOpen (α ⁻¹ᵁ AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 g) := by
  have : IsAffine (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 g).toScheme :=
    AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.isAffineOpen_basicOpen 𝒜 g hg hd
  have := isClosedImmersion_restrict_basicOpen 𝒜 α hcob
  exact (IsClosedImmersion.isAffine_surjective_of_isAffine
    (α ∣_ AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 g)).1

/-- **Every section of the chart is the image of a section of the standard open.** Through
`AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpenIsoAway` the sections of `D₊(g)` are the fractions `b / g^k` with
`b` homogeneous of degree `k · d`, so this is the surjectivity that lets the algebra generators of
the chart be written as such fractions — the second half of step 1 of [Stacks, Tag 02NP].

The statement is `Stacks.Immersion.surjective_app_of_le_coborderRange` at the standard open. -/
theorem surjective_app_basicOpen {d : ℕ} {g : A} (hg : g ∈ 𝒜 d) (hd : 0 < d)
    (hcob : AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 g ≤ α.coborderRange) :
    Function.Surjective (α.app (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 g)).hom :=
  Stacks.Immersion.surjective_app_of_le_coborderRange α _
    (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.isAffineOpen_basicOpen 𝒜 g hg hd) hcob

omit [IsImmersion α] in
/-- **The charts of the chosen degree-one coordinates cover `X`.** If the standard opens
`D₊(g_j)` have preimages covering `X` and every `g_j` is homogeneous of positive degree and lies
in the subalgebra generated over `A₀` by the family `y`, then the charts `α⁻¹(D₊(y_i))` cover `X`
as well.

This is what makes the family of global sections attached to the `y_i` — the sections of
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.MorphismsIntoProj.psiPullbackHom`, whose nonvanishing locus is
`α⁻¹(D₊(y_i))` by
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.MorphismsIntoProj.nonvanishingLocus_psiPullbackHom_one` — generate every
stalk, which is the generation clause of
`Stacks.VeryAmpleAffineBase.ProjCoordinateImmersion` at the coordinates the source chooses. -/
theorem exists_mem_preimage_basicOpen_of_mem_adjoin {ι : Type*} (y : ι → A)
    (hy : ∀ i, ∃ n, y i ∈ 𝒜 n) {m : ℕ} {d : Fin m → ℕ} {g : Fin m → A} (hd : ∀ j, 0 < d j)
    (hg : ∀ j, g j ∈ 𝒜 (d j)) (hmem : ∀ j, g j ∈ Algebra.adjoin (𝒜 0) (Set.range y))
    (hcov : ∀ x : X, ∃ j, x ∈ α ⁻¹ᵁ AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (g j)) (x : X) :
    ∃ i, x ∈ α ⁻¹ᵁ AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (y i) := by
  obtain ⟨j, hj⟩ := hcov x
  have h : α.base x ∈ ⨆ i, AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (y i) :=
    basicOpen_le_iSup_basicOpen_of_mem_adjoin 𝒜 y hy (hd j) (hg j) (hmem j) hj
  obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := TopologicalSpace.Opens.mem_iSup.mp h
  exact ⟨i, hi⟩

end Cover

/-! ### The algebra generators of a chart, as fractions -/

section Generators

variable {A : Type u} {σ : Type w} [CommRing A] [SetLike σ A] [AddSubgroupClass σ A]
  (𝒜 : ℕ → σ) [GradedRing 𝒜] {X S : Scheme.{u}}
  (α : X ⟶ AlgebraicGeometry.Proj 𝒜) [IsImmersion α]

/-- **A fraction `b / g^k` read as a function on the chart `α⁻¹(D₊(g))`**: the canonical map
`(A_g)₀ ⟶ Γ(Proj A, D₊(g))` of `AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.awayToSection` followed by `α` on
sections. -/
def awayToChart (g : A) :
    HomogeneousLocalization.Away 𝒜 g →+*
      Γ(X, α ⁻¹ᵁ AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 g) :=
  (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.awayToSection 𝒜 g ≫
    α.app (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 g)).hom

/-- **Every section of the chart is a fraction.** `AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.awayToSection` is an
isomorphism for `g` homogeneous of positive degree, and `α` is surjective on sections over a
standard open inside the coborder of its range. -/
theorem surjective_awayToChart {d : ℕ} {g : A} (hg : g ∈ 𝒜 d) (hd : 0 < d)
    (hcob : AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 g ≤ α.coborderRange) :
    Function.Surjective (awayToChart 𝒜 α g) := by
  have hiso : IsIso (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.awayToSection 𝒜 g) := by
    rw [← AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpenIsoAway_hom 𝒜 g hg hd]
    infer_instance
  exact (surjective_app_basicOpen 𝒜 α hg hd hcob).comp
    (ConcreteCategory.bijective_of_isIso (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.awayToSection 𝒜 g)).2

/-- **Step 1 of what [Stacks, Tag 02NP] still owes, completed: the algebra generators of each
chart are fractions `b / g^k`.** For `f : X ⟶ S` locally of finite type, `V` an affine open of
the base containing the image of the chart `α⁻¹(D₊(g))` of a standard open inside the coborder of
the range of `α`, there are finitely many elements of `(A_g)₀` whose images, together with the
sections coming from the base, generate every section of the chart.

This is [Stacks, Tag 01T2] — `AlgebraicGeometry.HasRingHomProperty.appLE` for
`AlgebraicGeometry.LocallyOfFiniteType`, the chart being affine by
`Stacks.CoordinateChoice.isAffineOpen_preimage_basicOpen` — fed through the surjectivity
`Stacks.CoordinateChoice.surjective_awayToChart`. The numerator and denominator of each generator
are `HomogeneousLocalization.num` and `HomogeneousLocalization.den`, the latter a power of `g`;
feeding them and `g` itself to `Stacks.CoordinateChoice.exists_fin_mem_adjoin_range` is the
source's choice of degree-one coordinates. -/
theorem exists_finset_away_forall_mem_closure (f : X ⟶ S) [LocallyOfFiniteType f] {d : ℕ} {g : A}
    (hg : g ∈ 𝒜 d) (hd : 0 < d)
    (hcob : AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 g ≤ α.coborderRange) {V : S.Opens}
    (hV : IsAffineOpen V) (hle : α ⁻¹ᵁ AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 g ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ V) :
    ∃ t : Finset (HomogeneousLocalization.Away 𝒜 g),
      ∀ z : Γ(X, α ⁻¹ᵁ AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 g), z ∈ Subring.closure
        (Set.range (f.appLE V (α ⁻¹ᵁ AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 g) hle).hom ∪
          awayToChart 𝒜 α g '' (t : Set (HomogeneousLocalization.Away 𝒜 g))) := by
  classical
  have hft : RingHom.FiniteType
      (f.appLE V (α ⁻¹ᵁ AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 g) hle).hom :=
    AlgebraicGeometry.HasRingHomProperty.appLE @LocallyOfFiniteType f ‹_› ⟨V, hV⟩
      ⟨_, isAffineOpen_preimage_basicOpen 𝒜 α hg hd hcob⟩ hle
  obtain ⟨t₀, ht₀⟩ := Stacks.ChartImmersionFinish.exists_finset_forall_mem_closure _ hft
  obtain ⟨sec, hsec⟩ := (surjective_awayToChart 𝒜 α hg hd hcob).hasRightInverse
  refine ⟨t₀.image sec, fun z =>
    Subring.closure_mono (Set.union_subset_union_right _ fun w hw => ?_) (ht₀ z)⟩
  exact ⟨sec w, by simpa using Finset.mem_image_of_mem sec hw, hsec w⟩

end Generators

end Stacks.CoordinateChoice

